cves.impact:
This vulnerability may allow remote attackers to cause a denial-of-service (DoS) on the NGINX system or to possibly trigger a code execution. There is no control plane exposure; this is a data plane issue only.

For example, the following configuration would be vulnerable because the js_fetch_proxy directive is configured with at least one client-controlled NGINX variable ($http_x_user and $http_x_password):

server {
    listen 127.0.0.1:8080;
    server_name localhost;       

    location / {
            # Client controlled variable expansion into URL contents
            # Example below x-user and x-password headers are used to construct the proxy URL
            # main.fetcher is a JavaScript function defined in the js file that calls ngx.fetch with the constructed URL
            js_fetch_proxy http://$http_x_user:$http_x_password@127.0.0.1:3128;
            js_content main.fetcher;
    }
 }
